{
  "name": "[TEST] Loss.Targets has no incoming connection",
  "description": "Compile-gate test fixture for the 2026-04-17 pin-connectivity check. Identical to mnist_mlp.cyxgraph except the DataInput.Labels \u2192 Loss.Targets wire is removed, leaving Loss.Targets with no incoming link. Loading this and hitting Compile should fail with: 'Required input pin Targets on node CrossEntropy has no incoming connection'. Before the check landed, this graph compiled fine and silently trained against whatever the executor read from the registry \u2014 exactly the 'pin is fooling user' case.",
  "parameters": []
}

{
  "name": "[TEST] Loss.Targets wired to model output instead of labels",
  "description": "Compile-gate test fixture for the 2026-04-17 pin-connectivity check. Loss.Targets HAS an incoming wire \u2014 but it's wired to fc3.Output (a model layer's tensor) instead of DataInput.Labels. Required-input check passes. The reachability check fails: 'Loss node CrossEntropy has its Targets pin wired, but the upstream chain never passes through a Labels-typed pin'. Before the check landed, this graph would compile fine and train against its own predictions as labels \u2014 silent gradient garbage with no error.",
  "parameters": []
}

{
  "name": "[TEST] Loss.Predictions wired to label stream instead of model",
  "description": "Compile-gate test fixture for the 2026-04-17 Predictions-reachability check. Loss.Predictions HAS an incoming wire \u2014 but it's wired to DataInput.Labels (the label stream) instead of the model's output. Required-input check passes. Reachability fails: 'Loss node CrossEntropy has its Predictions pin wired, but the upstream chain never passes through a model layer or Output node'. Before the check landed, this graph would compile and 'train' the loss on labels-vs-labels \u2014 perfect 0 loss with no learning, no error.",
  "parameters": []
}

{
  "name": "[TEST] Optimizer.Loss wired to a model output instead of a loss node",
  "description": "Compile-gate test fixture for the 2026-04-17 Optimizer-reachability check. Optimizer.Loss IS wired \u2014 but to fc3.Output (a Dense layer tensor) instead of CrossEntropy.Loss. The 'Tensor is universal' rule lets ImNodes accept the Tensor\u2192Loss link, and the required-input check passes. Reachability fails: 'Optimizer node Adam has its Loss pin wired, but the upstream chain never passes through a loss function'. Before this check landed, the optimizer would backprop from a random tensor with no error.",
  "parameters": []
}

